{#-
  Spiko: push the payment stablecoin to a Spiko deposit address.

  Spiko assigns each account a deposit address. Stablecoins sent there are
  invested in the fund at the next NAV. Redemptions are requested through
  Spiko's API and paid back as stablecoins from the same address. Neither leg
  needs a contract call from the Safe: sending is a plain ERC-20 `transfer`,
  receiving needs no permission.

  The role gets exactly one thing: `transfer` on the payment asset, recipient
  limited to the listed deposit addresses. No approve, no other token, no ETH,
  no delegatecall.

  Params
    payment_asset          Token alias key, e.g. "USDC". Resolved via
                           aliases.tokens[<key>]; unknown key fails at render.
    subscription_addresses Deposit addresses Spiko assigned to this account,
                           usually one. Each entry is a place the payment asset
                           can leave the Safe with no further approval, so list
                           only addresses Spiko actually assigned. Literals or
                           deployment-local aliases, not curated ones.

  Output
    payment asset: transfer(to in subscription_addresses, value: any),
    execution_options "none".
-#}
roles:
  - address: "{{ aliases.tokens[payment_asset] }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function transfer(address to, uint256 value)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: to
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "oneOf"
            values:
              {%- for addr in subscription_addresses %}
              - "{{ addr }}"
              {%- endfor %}
            value_type: "address"
          - name: value
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
